      "writtenOn": "2023-12-12T19:05:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, I should\u0027ve checked before. From Android 10, any device that ships Vulkan 1.1 is required to support the VK_ANDROID_external_memory_android_hardware_buffer:\nhttps://source.android.com/docs/compatibility/10/android-10-cdd\n\nHowever we only enforce API level 26 to include AHWB files which corresponds to Android 8 (https://apilevels.com/), so we should still check even though modern devices should theoretically support it.\n\nI don\u0027t think we plan on raising the minimum Android API level for using graphite, but if we did, that is what would allow us to skip that check.\n\nThank you!",
      "parentUuid": "0a00817e_67950f54",
